# grid2 = [[1,1,-1],[1,-1,1],[-1,1,1]]
# print(sol.cherryPickup(grid2))  # Output: 0
```

This solution efficiently calculates the maximum number of cherries that can be collected by two agents moving simultaneously on the grid. The time complexity is O(n^3) and the space complexity is also O(n^3), which is feasible given the constraint `1 <= n <= 50`.

