Then, it iterates over the grid from bottom-right to top-left, checking for the largest possible square subgrid with 1s on its border. The size of the square is determined by the minimum of the horizontal and vertical counts at each position, and it checks if such a square can be formed by verifying the horizontal and vertical counts at the opposite corners of the square. The maximum side length of such a square is kept track of, and the area of the largest square is returned.

