# print(sol.maxStudents([["#",".","#","#",".","#"],
#                        [".","#","#","#","#","."],
#                        ["#",".","#","#",".","#"]]))  # Output: 4
```

This solution efficiently computes the maximum number of students that can be seated without cheating using dynamic programming and bit masking. The constraints of the problem (with `m` and `n` up to 8) make this approach feasible.

