        while left < right:
            mid = (left + right) // 2
            # Number of missing integers up to arr[mid] is arr[mid] - (mid + 1)
            missing = arr[mid] - (mid + 1)

            if missing < k:
                left = mid + 1
            else:
                right = mid

        # After the loop, left is the smallest index such that the number of missing integers up to arr[left] is at least k
        # The kth missing number is then k more than the number of integers up to the previous index (left - 1)
        return left + k
```

This binary search approach has a time complexity of O(log n), making it more efficient for larger inputs.

