from typing import List

class Solution:
    def findChampion(self, n: int, edges: List[List[int]]) -> int:
        # Initialize a set to keep track of all teams that have incoming edges
        has_incoming_edge = set()

        # Populate the set with all nodes that have incoming edges
        for u, v in edges:
            has_incoming_edge.add(v)

        # The champion will be the node with no incoming edges
        champions = [i for i in range(n) if i not in has_incoming_edge]

        # If there is exactly one such node, it is the champion
        if len(champions) == 1:
            return champions[0]
        else:
            return -1
```

This solution works by identifying all nodes that have incoming edges. The champion node will be the one that does not have any incoming edges, as it is not weaker than any other team. If there is exactly one such node, it is returned as the champion. If there are multiple or no such nodes, the function returns -1.

